---
export const title = 'Export';
export const order = 530;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';

import dataSource from '../_data-source.json';
---

<p>
  <code>exportCsv(options)</code> returns the rows as CSV text (RFC 4180: fields with a comma, quote
  or line break are quoted, lines end in CRLF). The first line holds the column labels. By default
  it exports the visible columns in display order and the rows on the current page, in the current
  sort and grouping. Options:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>allRows</code>: every row, not only the current page.</li>
  <li><code>columns</code>: column names to export, in that order, hidden columns included.</li>
  <li><code>filename</code>: the file name for <code>downloadCsv()</code> (default <code>table.csv</code>).</li>
</ul>
<p>
  A cell holds the column's <code>exportValue(row)</code> when it has one, else the raw field value
  (dates as ISO strings, objects as JSON). <code>downloadCsv(options)</code> saves the same text as
  a UTF-8 file through a Blob URL. A managed table exports the <code>data</code> it has. Values are
  written as they are: if the file is opened in a spreadsheet and values come from users, guard
  against formulas (text starting with <code>=</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>-</code> or
  <code>@</code>) in <code>exportValue</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang='html'>
  <div style='width: 100%; height: 20rem;'>
    <wc-table id='table-export' key-field='_id' label='People'>
      <wc-pagination slot='footer' page-size='5' page-sizes='[5, 10]'></wc-pagination>
    </wc-table>
  </div>
  <wc-button id='export-download' variant='outlined' size='sm'>
    <wc-icon slot='icon' name='download'></wc-icon>
    Download all rows
  </wc-button>
  <pre id='export-output' class='text-body-small'></pre>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ dataSource }}>
    const $table = document.getElementById('table-export');
    $table.columns = [
      { name: 'name', label: 'Name', width: 14 },
      { name: 'company', label: 'Company', width: 12 },
      { name: 'balance', label: 'Balance', width: 10, exportValue: row => row.balance.replace(/[$,]/g, '') },
    ];
    $table.data = dataSource;
    const show = () => {
      document.getElementById('export-output').textContent = $table.exportCsv();
    };
    customElements.whenDefined('wc-table').then(() => requestAnimationFrame(show));
    $table.addEventListener('page', () => requestAnimationFrame(show));
    document
      .getElementById('export-download')
      .addEventListener('click', () => $table.downloadCsv({ allRows: true, filename: 'people.csv' }));
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
